const blog=()=>pageShell(`<section class="section"><div class="wrap article-grid"><article class="article-card" tabindex="0"><span>BENCHMARK</span><h2>LoCoMo evidence retrieval.</h2><p>A frozen run, its result, and every caveat needed to interpret it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/blog/locomo-benchmark">Read the report →</a></article><article class="article-card muted-card" tabindex="0"><span>ENGINEERING</span><h2>Build notes.</h2><p>Releases and implementation work live with the code.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Lians-ai/Lians" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open GitHub ↗</a></article></div></section>`);
const benchmark=()=>pageShell(`<section class="section benchmark-report"><div class="wrap"><header class="benchmark-report-head"><div><h2>A frozen, reproducible retrieval run.</h2><p>The Lians retrieval and context pipeline found at least one gold evidence turn for 1,498 of 1,536 answerable LoCoMo questions.</p></div><div class="benchmark-seal"><strong>PASS</strong><small>10 conversations · 4 categories</small></div></header><div class="benchmark-metrics"><article><strong>97.53%</strong><span>raw evidence hit</span></article><article><strong>97.53%</strong><span>compiled evidence hit</span></article><article><strong>100%</strong><span>retrieved-hit retention</span></article><article><strong>0</strong><span>packs over 1,200 tokens</span></article></div><div class="benchmark-detail"><main class="prose"><h2>What the score measures.</h2><p>For each answerable question, Lians retrieves up to 200 semantic candidates. A frozen reranker adds dialogue support, then the context compiler selects up to 50 attributed memory bundles within a 1,200-token estimate. A question counts as a hit when the final context contains at least one dataset-identified evidence turn.</p><div class="benchmark-warning"><b>This is not 97.53% answer accuracy.</b><p>No model generated answers and no LLM judge graded them. This result isolates evidence retrieval and context compilation.</p></div><h2>Leakage boundary.</h2><p>The retriever receives the conversation and question only. Gold evidence IDs and reference answers enter after retrieval solely to calculate the score. They never affect retrieval, reranking, dialogue bundling, or context selection.</p><h2>Category results.</h2><div class="category-bars"><div><span>Single-hop</span><i style="--score:98.69%"></i><b>98.69%</b></div><div><span>Temporal</span><i style="--score:97.82%"></i><b>97.82%</b></div><div><span>Multi-hop</span><i style="--score:96.45%"></i><b>96.45%</b></div><div><span>Open-domain</span><i style="--score:89.13%"></i><b>89.13%</b></div></div><p class="benchmark-caveat">The 95+ gate applies to the overall score across all answerable categories. Open-domain is shown separately because it remains the weakest category.</p><h2>Reproduce it.</h2><p>The dated run used Lians' public LoCoMo exporter plus the frozen scorer and strict verifier described here. The verifier requires all 1,536 answerable questions, all four categories, at least 95% raw and compiled evidence hit, 100% retention, and zero over-budget contexts.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/Lians-ai/Lians/tree/master/agentmem/benchmarks" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect benchmark source ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Lians-ai/Lians" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open Lians on GitHub ↗</a></div></main><aside class="benchmark-protocol"><dl><div><dt>Questions</dt><dd>1,536</dd></div><div><dt>Retrieval</dt><dd>semantic top-200</dd></div><div><dt>Context</dt><dd>radius ±2</dd></div><div><dt>Compiler</dt><dd>top-50 fair-share</dd></div><div><dt>Budget</dt><dd>1,200 tokens</dd></div><div><dt>Mean context</dt><dd>1,084 tokens</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence hits</dt><dd>1,498</dd></div></dl><small>Category 5 is adversarial/unanswerable and excluded under the standard answerable-question protocol.</small></aside></div></div></section>`);
const judgedScoreNote=()=>`<div class="answer-score-note"><strong>92.9%</strong><div><b>LLM-judged answer accuracy</b><p>1,540 LoCoMo questions · top-200 · GPT-5 answerer and judge · unmodified mem0ai/memory-benchmarks harness.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Lians-ai/Lians/blob/master/agentmem/docs/benchmarks/locomo-judged-2026-07-09.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Judged protocol and category results ↗</a></div></div>`;
